node_modules/
dist/
data/
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/data
# TypeScript incremental build state. It has to go wherever dist goes:
# left in the context it arrives in the image while dist does not, so tsc
# reads it, concludes the output is current, and emits nothing - and the
# build then fails on the missing declarations. Git ignores these too, so a
# build from a clean export never hit it; one from a working tree does.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.scratch
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
.references/
.agent/
.gemini/
.vscode/
.idea/
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
*.md
*.log
coverage/
tests/
unraid/
docker/
.cache/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
